    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95532" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμῠγερός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μογερός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with
				pain, painful</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1065
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.374
			</span></i>: Adv., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				4.380
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμυγερὸν σμυγερῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					166
				</span></i>
			 (anap.), as Brunck for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στυγερὸν
				στυγερῶς</span>; cf. Sch.ad loc., <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1463.44
			</span></i>:—<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> has only the compd. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισμυγερῶς</span> (q.v.).</div>
